            <ArticleTitle>[Abortive duplication of the gut (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1055-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Presentation of a case of intestinal duplication sited in the rectosigmoid colon. Rectosigmoid colon and duplication were coated with gastric mucosa. Diagnosis of heterotopic gastric mucosa was done by biopsy and 99mTc-pertechnetate scintigraphy. The diseased colon was removed by Rehbein pull-through procedure. Complete removal was proved by clinical course and scintigraphy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
